## Original Content
<p>In addition to data protection, the EU’s General Data Protection Regulation requires businesses to ensure consumers can exercise their data privacy rights. But first, individuals must know these rights.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://gdpr.eu/consumers-gdpr-data-privacy-rights/">Do consumers know their GDPR data privacy rights?</a> appeared first on <a href="https://gdpr.eu">GDPR.eu</a>.</p>

## Summary
The article discusses the EU's GDPR requirement for businesses to enable consumers to exercise their data privacy rights, but emphasizes that individuals must first know these rights. It highlights the potential gap in consumer awareness regarding GDPR provisions.

## Key Points
- GDPR mandates businesses to ensure consumers can exercise data privacy rights.
- Individuals need to know their data privacy rights to exercise them.
- Consumer awareness of GDPR rights may be insufficient.
- The regulation focuses on both data protection and facilitating access to rights.


